RISC3D test kit 36 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

RISC3D now lives as !RISC3D in !Boot.Resources: the RISC3D module, and
a folder GPU holding the GPU driver for the machine. A program's !Run
needs only

  RMEnsure RISC3D 0.04 RMLoad RISC3D:RISC3D

and RISC3D 0.04 loads the driver from GPU itself: it tries each module
there until one starts (a driver refuses to start where its GPU isn't).
riscos-risc3d 0.20-1 installs !RISC3D with Linux3D in GPU.

On RISC OS on Linux (RiSH's Root shell)
-----------------------------------
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 34.
 2. apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.20-1_arm64.deb
 3. Restart (shut down and switch on).
 4. Double-click Auto. It shows RISC3D as loaded at start-up, then
    reloads it with nothing but RMLoad RISC3D:RISC3D (Linux3D should be
    loaded again from GPU by RISC3D), and draws through it.
 5. Optional: Test, Cube and Lit as before.

On native RISC OS on the Pi 4 (optional)
----------------------------------------
 1. Copy !RISC3D from this kit into !Boot.Resources (its GPU is empty).
 2. Copy V3DRender's module into !RISC3D.GPU.
 3. Double-click !RISC3D, then at the command line:
      RMLoad RISC3D:RISC3D
      RISC3D
    It should say "Driver: V3DRender..." and list V3DRender as registered
    under "Drivers folder". With GPU empty it says no driver is
    registered (programs then draw in software).

